Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:42:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] refactor(cadapter): merge duplicate S3 multipart
 implementations

Closes #10 (gqf2008/brewfs)

multipart_upload (single buffer) and multipart_upload_vectored had near-
identical create/upload/complete/cleanup/retry flows with only the body
construction differing.

- New shared multipart_upload_parts: creates the upload, uploads
  part-sized Vec<Bytes> groups concurrently (same semaphore + per-part
  retry policy), completes, and arms the abort-on-drop guard.
- multipart_upload builds parts from &[u8]; multipart_upload_vectored
  keeps its chunk coalescing and both delegate to the shared pipeline.
- Behavior unchanged: same part boundaries, request shapes, MD5 and
  payload-checksum handling; existing s3 unit tests pass.
